  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "Separating things into how a component is set up would be pretty important with the upcoming update. \n\nAn example of this would be non-important vs important lights.\n\nVRChat's performance rating system currently clumps things like the above mentioned non-imporant, and important lights into the same \"Lights\" category. \nThis means that even a non imporant light will mark you as \"Poor\" even with the considerably decreased performance cost. \n\nThere are probably other components that have similar options that would increase or decrease performance. \n\nThe gist is, things that get clumped together when trying to give the end user more information, and ultimately, misinformation, should be changed.",
